          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ci_pipeline_invariance_audit(series_vals, window: int, t0: int, center_flag: bool) -> tuple[float, bool]:\n    arr = np.asarray(series_vals, dtype=float)\n    def roll_mean(x):\n        out = np.empty_like(x)\n        n = len(x)\n        half = window // 2\n        for i in range(n):\n            if center_flag:\n                lo, hi = max(0, i - half), min(n, i + half + 1)\n            else:\n                lo, hi = max(0, i - window + 1), i + 1\n            out[i] = float(np.mean(x[lo:hi]))\n        return out\n    base = roll_mean(arr)\n    pert = arr.copy()\n    pert[t0 + 1 :] *= 50.0\n    after = roll_mean(pert)\n    max_past_delta = float(np.max(np.abs(base[: t0 + 1] - after[: t0 + 1])))\n    is_causal = bool(max_past_delta == 0.0)\n    return (round(max_past_delta, 4), is_causal)\n```"
